  <!-- ==================== PAGE 2: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & ARCHITECTURE ==================== -->
  <div class="page">
    <h1>1. Executive Summary & Architecture Overview</h1>
    
    <p>
      <strong>MediAI</strong> is an end-to-end, full-stack hospital clinical triage and patient prioritization system engineered according to modern hospital emergency department protocols (Emergency Severity Index / Canadian Triage Acuity Scale). It bridges high-throughput front-end clinical workflows with persistent relational storage and multi-domain AI explainability.
    </p>

    <h2>1.1 Approved Technology Stack Alignment</h2>
    <p>
      The system strictly adheres to the approved capstone toolset requirements, ensuring full compliance without disallowed dependencies:
    </p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Tier</th>
          <th>Technology</th>
          <th>Version / Specification</th>
          <th>Role in System</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Front-End</strong></td>
          <td>HTML5, Vanilla CSS3, Modern JavaScript</td>
          <td>ECMAScript 2022 / CSS Variables</td>
          <td>Accessible, high-performance UI matching clinical terminal guidelines without third-party design bloat.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Templates</strong></td>
          <td>Thymeleaf & Static Resource Engines</td>
          <td>Spring Boot 3.3.4 Starter</td>
          <td>Dual-serving of clinical views (intake terminal, queue, doctor workstation, analytics).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Back-End</strong></td>
          <td>Java Core, Spring Boot RESTful Web Services</td>
          <td>Java 17 (LTS), Spring Boot 3.3.4</td>
          <td>Enterprise service architecture, dependency injection, and deterministic clinical engines.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>ORM & Persistence</strong></td>
          <td>Spring Data JPA & Hibernate Core</td>
          <td>Hibernate 6.5.3, JPA 3.1</td>
          <td>Entity-relational mapping, transactional data consistency, derived queries, and relationship integrity.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
          <td>MySQL Relational Database Server</td>
          <td>MySQL 8.0+ / InnoDB Engine</td>
          <td>Persistent, ACID-compliant transactional storage for patients, vitals, triage records, and audit journals.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Build & Lifecycle</strong></td>
          <td>Apache Maven</td>
          <td>Maven 3.9+ via <span class="code-pill">mvnw</span> wrapper</td>
          <td>Dependency resolution, multi-stage compilation, and automated test execution.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>1.2 Core Architectural Principles & Strict UI Preservation</h2>
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>Zero UI Disruption Mandate:</strong> All new capabilities (Voice Input, Notifications, 2-Step OTP, Feedback Ratings, and AI Clinical Chatbot) are added in a 100% backward-compatible manner. Existing layouts, colors, fonts, routes, and triage risk algorithms remain completely intact.
    </div>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Deterministic Safety First:</strong> Machine learning inferences are strictly bounded by hard deterministic physiological tripwires (e.g., SpO2 &lt; 90% immediately overrides all models to P1 Critical).</li>
      <li><strong>Zero Protected Health Information (PHI) Leakage:</strong> Patient names are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM. Medical Record Numbers (MRNs) use SHA-256 salted hashes. System audit journals log zero raw patient health identifiers.</li>
      <li><strong>Bilingual Clinical Accessibility:</strong> Full dynamic language interchange between English (<span class="code-pill">en-US</span>) and Tamil (<span class="code-pill">ta-IN</span>) across user interfaces, voice recognition, and clinical reassurance output.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>1.3 System Component Architecture</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Clinical Decision Support Layer</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>TriageEngineService:</strong> Computes scaled risk scores (0-100) and priority categories (P1 to P4).<br>
          • <strong>GeminiAiService:</strong> Evaluates prompt-guarded contextual clinical rationale.<br>
          • <strong>TreeSHAP Factor Breakdown:</strong> Transparent attribution weights explaining why an acuity tier was assigned.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Security & Audit Layer</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>JwtAuthFilter & SecurityConfig:</strong> Stateless bearer token management.<br>
          • <strong>AuthService & OTP Engine:</strong> SHA-256 hashed 2-factor passcodes with 5-min timeout and attempt limiting.<br>
          • <strong>AuditService:</strong> Immutable journal logging actor roles, IP addresses, and encrypted action categories.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 3: FEATURE 1 & FEATURE 2 ==================== -->
  <div class="page">
    <h1>2. Review of Core Features: Feature 1 & Feature 2</h1>

    <h2>2.1 Feature 1: Voice Input for Clinical Symptoms</h2>
    <p>
      The voice recognition module enables patients and triage triage nurses to dictate acute symptoms hands-free, which is especially vital in emergency triage where manual keyboard entry can cause critical intake delays.
    </p>

    <div class="callout callout-success">
      <strong>Implementation Location:</strong> Integrated seamlessly adjacent to the chief complaint input field in <span class="code-pill">intake.html</span> (line 230) and <span class="code-pill">profile.html</span> (line 112) via a compact microphone button (<span class="code-pill">btn btn-outline btn-sm</span>).
    </div>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Requirement</th>
          <th>Implementation Mechanism</th>
          <th>Verification Status</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Bilingual Speech Recognition</strong></td>
          <td>Leverages Web Speech API (<span class="code-pill">MediAPI.voice.createRecognizer</span>) configured to stream either <span class="code-pill">en-US</span> or <span class="code-pill">ta-IN</span> dynamically based on active language selection.</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-low">Verified</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Editable Confirmation</strong></td>
          <td>Transcribed speech streams into the editable <span class="code-pill">ptComplaint</span> text input. Patients and nurses can review, adjust, or delete text before advancing. Speech is never submitted automatically.</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-low">Verified</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Manual Typing Fallback</strong></td>
          <td>Input field retains standard keyboard focus. Manual typing remains 100% available without interruption.</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-low">Verified</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Permission & Error Safety</strong></td>
          <td>Catches <span class="code-pill">not-allowed</span>, <span class="code-pill">no-speech</span>, and unsupported browser states with polite inline non-blocking guidance banners.</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-low">Verified</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Preservation of Triage Logic</strong></td>
          <td>Captured text flows into the existing <span class="code-pill">POST /api/v1/triage/assess</span> pipeline without altering clinical calculations.</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-low">Verified</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>2.2 Feature 2: Real-Time Clinical Notifications & Alerts System</h2>
    <p>
      A persistent, role-aware notification subsystem provides automated clinical alerts for intake completion, triage tier status updates, resuscitation red flags, and doctor override events.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Database & Entity Structure</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>Entity:</strong> <span class="code-pill">Notification.java</span> mapping to table <span class="code-pill">notifications</span>.<br>
          • <strong>Fields:</strong> <span class="code-pill">id</span>, <span class="code-pill">targetRole</span> (ALL, DOCTOR, NURSE), <span class="code-pill">title</span>, <span class="code-pill">message</span>, <span class="code-pill">priority</span> (CRITICAL, HIGH, INFO), <span class="code-pill">isRead</span>, <span class="code-pill">referenceId</span>, <span class="code-pill">createdAt</span>.<br>
          • <strong>Repository:</strong> <span class="code-pill">NotificationRepository.java</span> supporting unread counting and role filtering.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>UI Top-Nav Bell Drawer</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>Global Injector:</strong> <span class="code-pill">MediAPI.initNotifications()</span> auto-mounts a bell (<span class="code-pill">🔔</span>) in <span class="code-pill">.nav-actions</span> on every page.<br>
          • <strong>Badge:</strong> Real-time unread counter pill.<br>
          • <strong>Drawer:</strong> Interactive dropdown showing timestamps, priority color indicators, individual "Mark read" triggers, and "Mark all read" button.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Automated Alert Triggers Workflow</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Clinical Trigger Event</th>
          <th>Target Role</th>
          <th>Priority Tier</th>
          <th>Notification Content</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Patient Intake Assessment Completed</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-info">ALL</span></td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-moderate">INFO</span></td>
          <td>"New Triage Assessment Recorded with [Category] priority."</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tier-1 Hard Red Flag / Critical Hypoxia Triggered</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-critical">DOCTOR / NURSE</span></td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-critical">CRITICAL</span></td>
          <td>"🚨 CRITICAL Triage Alert: Immediate resuscitation bay attention required."</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Physician Overrides AI Triage Classification</td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-high">ALL</span></td>
          <td><span class="badge badge-high">HIGH</span></td>
          <td>"👨‍⚕️ Physician Triage Override: Category updated to [Target Category]."</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 4: FEATURE 3 & FEATURE 4 ==================== -->
  <div class="page">
    <h1>3. Review of Core Features: Feature 3 & Feature 4</h1>

    <h2>3.1 Feature 3: Login Authentication, Role Authorization & 2-Step OTP Security</h2>
    <p>
      Staff authentication portal (<span class="code-pill">signin.html</span>) provides enterprise-grade Two-Step Verification (2FA) with cryptographically secure One-Time Passcodes (OTP) while completely preserving the existing visual layout.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Two-Step Verification Protocol</h3>
        <ol style="font-size: 8.5pt; margin-left: 1rem;">
          <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> User submits email and password. Server validates credentials against BCrypt hashes in MySQL.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Generates a 6-digit random passcode, cryptographically hashes it with SHA-256, and stores it in <span class="code-pill">user_otps</span> with a 5-minute expiry timestamp.</li>
          <li><strong>Client Challenge:</strong> Form transitions in-place to Step 2 showing masked email (<span class="code-pill">d***r@mediai.org</span>), countdown timer, and OTP input field.</li>
          <li><strong>Validation:</strong> Submitting OTP verifies hash match. Upon success, OTP is immediately invalidated and JWT token is issued.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Security Guardrails & Hardening</h3>
        <ul style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          <li><strong>Zero Cleartext Storage:</strong> Passcodes are hashed with SHA-256 before database insertion.</li>
          <li><strong>Attempt Limiting:</strong> Maximum 3 failed verification attempts before the session token is permanently revoked.</li>
          <li><strong>Single-Use Enforcement:</strong> Re-using a validated OTP returns HTTP 400 Bad Request.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend Rate Limiting:</strong> 60-second cooldown period prevents SMS/email flooding.</li>
          <li><strong>Backend RBAC:</strong> Endpoints enforce role verification via JWT claims and request headers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>3.2 Feature 4: Patient Care Experience & Feedback Ratings Registry</h2>
    <p>
      An integrated clinical quality rating and feedback subsystem allows patients and clinicians to submit verified care evaluations following triage intake without modifying medical calculations.
    </p>

    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>Clinical Fire-walling:</strong> Feedback scores and qualitative comments are strictly segregated from AI risk scores, TreeSHAP algorithms, and triage classifications. They are used purely for clinical operations and service quality telemetry.
    </div>

    <h3>Component Architecture</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Subsystem</th>
          <th>Implementation Details</th>
          <th>Location</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Feedback Form</strong></td>
          <td>Interactive 1-to-5 star rating selector + sanitized text comment area (capped at 1,000 characters to prevent buffer abuse). Appears immediately after triage calculation.</td>
          <td>Step 4 in <span class="code-pill">intake.html</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Persistent Entity</strong></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">Feedback.java</span> stored in MySQL <span class="code-pill">feedbacks</span> table with <span class="code-pill">rating</span>, <span class="code-pill">comment</span>, <span class="code-pill">submitterRole</span>, <span class="code-pill">category</span>, <span class="code-pill">createdAt</span>.</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">com.mediai.entity.Feedback</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Admin Telemetry Registry</strong></td>
          <td>Displays aggregate metrics: average star rating, total submission counter, star distribution percentage bars (5★ through 1★), and real-time qualitative comment list.</td>
          <td>Card in <span class="code-pill">analytics.html</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>REST Endpoints</strong></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST /api/v1/feedback</span> (submission) and <span class="code-pill">GET /api/v1/feedback/summary</span> (aggregation).</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">FeedbackController.java</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 5: FEATURE 5 & DATABASE SCHEMA ==================== -->
  <div class="page">
    <h1>4. Review of Feature 5 & Complete Database Schema</h1>

    <h2>4.1 Feature 5: Clinical AI Chatbot Assistant (MediAI Assistant)</h2>
    <p>
      A universal, non-intrusive floating clinical widget (<span class="code-pill">#mediaiChatbotLauncher</span>) mounted across all pages to guide patients and clinicians with symptom inquiries, normal vital sign baselines, and emergency triage navigation.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Clinical Intelligence & Safety Interception</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>Red-Flag Emergency Interception:</strong> Automatic real-time regex detection of life-threatening presentations (crushing chest pain, severe dyspnea, heavy hemorrhage, stroke symptoms) in English & Tamil.<br>
          • <strong>Emergency Directive:</strong> Immediately flags <span class="code-pill">is_emergency = true</span>, halts standard Q&A, and issues prominent directive to dial <strong>108 / 112 / 911</strong> or proceed directly to the Emergency Room.<br>
          • <strong>AI Generative + Clinical Fallback:</strong> Seamless fallback covering fever thresholds (&ge; 38.5°C), clinical pain scales (1-10), and vital signs baselines.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Interactive Widget Capabilities</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 8.5pt;">
          • <strong>Bilingual Interchange:</strong> Instant toggle between English (<span class="code-pill">EN</span>) and Tamil (<span class="code-pill">தமிழ்</span>) updating prompt context and chips.<br>
          • <strong>Integrated Voice Dictation:</strong> Built-in microphone button powered by Web Speech API allowing hands-free patient voice queries.<br>
          • <strong>Quick Action Chips:</strong> One-click prompts for common medical inquiries.<br>
          • <strong>Session Memory:</strong> Conversations persistently stored in MySQL <span class="code-pill">chat_messages</span> with history retrieval and clearing APIs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>4.2 Relational Database Schema Architecture (MySQL 8.0)</h2>
    <p>
      All data entities are managed using Hibernate with <span class="code-pill">spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update</span>, guaranteeing zero data loss on restart and maintaining relational integrity:
    </p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Table Name</th>
          <th>Primary Key</th>
          <th>Key Columns & Constraints</th>
          <th>Relational Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">patients</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">mrn_hash</span>, <span class="code-pill">encrypted_name</span>, <span class="code-pill">dob</span>, <span class="code-pill">gender</span></td>
          <td>Master patient demographics with AES-256 encrypted names.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">vital_signs</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">patient_id</span> (FK), <span class="code-pill">heart_rate</span>, <span class="code-pill">systolic_bp</span>, <span class="code-pill">spo2</span>, <span class="code-pill">temp</span></td>
          <td>Physiological vital readings with validation bounds.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">triage_assessments</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">patient_id</span> (FK), <span class="code-pill">vitals_id</span> (FK), <span class="code-pill">calculated_category</span>, <span class="code-pill">risk_score</span></td>
          <td>Acuity classification with TreeSHAP and AI rationale payloads.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">triage_reviews</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">assessment_id</span> (FK), <span class="code-pill">doctor_id</span>, <span class="code-pill">final_category</span>, <span class="code-pill">is_overridden</span></td>
          <td>Doctor overrides and clinical confirmation audits.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">notifications</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">target_role</span>, <span class="code-pill">title</span>, <span class="code-pill">message</span>, <span class="code-pill">priority</span>, <span class="code-pill">is_read</span></td>
          <td>Role-based persistent clinical alerts and triage updates.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">user_otps</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">temp_token</span> (IDX), <span class="code-pill">otp_hash</span>, <span class="code-pill">attempts</span>, <span class="code-pill">expires_at</span></td>
          <td>Single-use SHA-256 hashed 2FA passcode sessions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">feedbacks</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">rating</span> (1-5), <span class="code-pill">comment</span>, <span class="code-pill">submitter_role</span>, <span class="code-pill">reference_id</span></td>
          <td>Patient care experience and staff feedback records.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">chat_messages</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">conversation_id</span> (IDX), <span class="code-pill">sender</span>, <span class="code-pill">message</span> (TEXT), <span class="code-pill">is_emergency</span></td>
          <td>Bilingual clinical assistant conversation history.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">audit_logs</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">id</span> (VARCHAR 36)</td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">action_category</span>, <span class="code-pill">actor_id</span>, <span class="code-pill">ip_address</span>, <span class="code-pill">timestamp</span></td>
          <td>Zero-PHI append-only compliance journal trail.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 6: API CATALOG & VERIFICATION ==================== -->
  <div class="page">
    <h1>5. RESTful API Catalog & Verification Results</h1>

    <h2>5.1 Comprehensive RESTful Service Endpoints</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Method</th>
          <th>Endpoint Route</th>
          <th>Access / Role</th>
          <th>Description & Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/auth/login-step1</span></td>
          <td>Public</td>
          <td>Validates credentials; issues temp token & dispatches 6-digit OTP.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/auth/verify-otp</span></td>
          <td>Public</td>
          <td>Verifies OTP hash; enforces attempt limits; issues JWT session token.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/auth/resend-otp</span></td>
          <td>Public</td>
          <td>Issues replacement OTP with cooldown rate-limit verification.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/triage/assess</span></td>
          <td>Public / Intake</td>
          <td>Computes triage category, risk score, TreeSHAP & dispatches alert.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">GET</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/notifications</span></td>
          <td>Authenticated</td>
          <td>Retrieves notifications filtered by role (<span class="code-pill">?role=ALL/DOCTOR/NURSE</span>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">PUT</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/notifications/read-all</span></td>
          <td>Authenticated</td>
          <td>Marks all unread notifications as read.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/feedback</span></td>
          <td>Public / User</td>
          <td>Submits 1-5 star care rating and sanitized qualitative comment.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">GET</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/feedback/summary</span></td>
          <td>Admin / Staff</td>
          <td>Returns aggregate average, distribution bars, and recent comments.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/chat/message</span></td>
          <td>Public / Patient</td>
          <td>Interprets clinical query, intercepts red flags, returns AI reply.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="code-pill">POST</span></td>
          <td><span class="code-pill">/api/v1/doctor/override</span></td>
          <td>Doctor / Staff</td>
          <td>Physician confirmation/override with 15-char rationale safety check.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

